---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — DomainSifter"
  description="Plain-English terms covering acceptable use, affiliate disclosure, and limits of liability for DomainSifter."
  noindex={true}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500"><em>Last updated: April 2026</em></p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          By using DomainSifter (&ldquo;the service&rdquo;, &ldquo;the site&rdquo;), you agree to
          these terms. They're short and written in plain English on purpose.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">What DomainSifter is</h2>
        <p>
          DomainSifter publishes a daily-curated list of recently-expired
          domain names that appear to be available for registration. We filter
          out spam, malware, gibberish, and known abuse signals before
          publishing.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">What we don't guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Availability.</strong> We verify availability via RDAP at the moment we
          publish the list, but the actual availability of any specific domain
          can change between the moment we check and the moment you try to
          register it. A domain shown on our list may already be registered
          by someone else by the time you click through to a registrar.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Quality or value.</strong> We filter for spam and abuse, but we don't
          guarantee any domain on our list has commercial value, isn't
          trademarked, doesn't have a legal history, or won't have problems
          after registration. Do your own due diligence before purchasing.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Legal cleanliness.</strong> Some expired domains have legal history we
          can't detect (UDRP disputes, trademark conflicts, defamation history).
          We don't research individual domains for legal issues. If you register
          a domain that turns out to have legal problems, that's on you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-ink">Continuous availability.</strong> We try to publish daily but make no
          uptime guarantee. The service may be temporarily unavailable due
          to technical issues.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">Affiliate disclosure</h2>
        <p>
          When you click &ldquo;Register&rdquo; links on the site, you're taken to
          third-party domain registrars (Namecheap, NameSilo). We earn a
          commission when you register a domain via these links. This
          commission doesn't affect the price you pay — it's paid by the
          registrar from their margin.
        </p>
        <p>
          This means DomainSifter has a financial interest in users registering
          domains via our links. The list itself is filtered honestly regardless
          of which registrars we have affiliate relationships with — we don't
          prioritize or hide domains based on commission rates.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          You may use DomainSifter freely for personal or commercial domain
          research. You may NOT:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 marker:text-stone-400">
          <li>Scrape the site at high frequency or in ways that disrupt service</li>
          <li>Republish our daily list as your own without attribution</li>
          <li>Use the service for any illegal purpose</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We reserve the right to block access to anyone violating these rules.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The service is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; without warranty of any kind. We
          make no guarantees about uptime, accuracy, completeness, or fitness
          for any particular purpose.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, the operator of DomainSifter
          is not liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential
          damages arising from your use of the service. This includes (but is
          not limited to) financial loss from unavailable domains, legal issues
          with registered domains, or business decisions based on data shown
          on the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you registered a domain via our links and it turned out to have
          problems, your recourse is with the domain registrar (where you paid
          for the domain) and any relevant legal body — not with DomainSifter.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by Estonian law. Any disputes will be
          resolved in Estonian courts.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms occasionally. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date
          at the top reflects the most recent change. Material changes will
          be communicated via the newsletter to existing subscribers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink pt-4">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about these terms:<br />
          <a href="mailto:hello@domainsifter.com" class="text-accent font-medium hover:underline">hello@domainsifter.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
